{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why your env vars resolve the same way whether you build from Xcode, the terminal, or CI."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation"],"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tightlip"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"How Environment Sourcing Works","role":"article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Env-var secret setups have a recurring failure mode: the variable works in your shell but Xcode can’t see it, or it works locally but not in CI, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" exports it fine but "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" from a launcher doesn’t pick it up."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tightlip addresses this by sourcing your shell init file itself, in a controlled subshell, every build.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The Algorithm","anchor":"The-Algorithm"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For each build, the plugin:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sources the env file in a clean zsh subshell."}]},{"type":"text","text":" By default this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~\/.zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":", sourced with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zsh -f"},{"type":"text","text":" (no startup files, no profile chain). The subshell captures the resulting environment as a snapshot."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Merges that snapshot with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — the build’s own environment, including Xcode Scheme env vars and CI job env vars."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Resolves per-key conflicts in favor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProcessInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A CI runner that explicitly exports "},{"code":"APP_API_KEY","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" overrides anything "},{"code":"~\/.zshenv","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" might have said."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The result: identical resolution regardless of how the build was launched. Xcode.app from Finder, Conductor, VS Code, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" from Terminal — same env vars seen, same generated file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Failure Modes","anchor":"Failure-Modes"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subshell sourcing has a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"5-second timeout"}]},{"type":"text","text":". If sourcing fails (the file doesn’t exist, the file errors out, or it just takes too long), the tool falls back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProcessInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" alone and writes a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"note:"},{"type":"text","text":" to stderr identifying the file."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This means CI runners with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"~\/.zshenv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" work unchanged — the fallback kicks in immediately and the job’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"env:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block is the sole source of values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Slow `.zshenv` Cases","anchor":"Slow-zshenv-Cases"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tools like ","type":"text"},{"code":"mise","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"asdf","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"direnv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" invoked during ","type":"text"},{"code":".zshenv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can push past the 5-second budget. If you see the ","type":"text"},{"code":"note: sourcing \/path\/to\/file ... using process environment only","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" message and weren’t expecting it, reproduce with:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"bash","code":["zsh -f -c 'source ~\/.zshenv'"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If that hangs or errors, your shell init is the cause. Move slow tools out of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zshenv"},{"type":"text","text":" (into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zshrc"},{"type":"text","text":", which the plugin doesn’t read), or point Tightlip at a smaller sidecar file with the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"envFile directive","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"envFile directive"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/environmentsourcing"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvironmentSourcing","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftPM build-tool plugin that generates a typed Swift "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Secrets"},{"type":"text","text":" enum from environment variables at build time."}],"title":"Tightlip","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/EnvFileDirective":{"title":"Overriding the Sourced Env File","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/envfiledirective","abstract":[{"text":"Point Tightlip at a different shell-init file with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"envFile:"},{"text":" directive.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/EnvFileDirective","type":"topic"},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/Obfuscation":{"title":"Obfuscation and Threat Model","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/obfuscation","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/Obfuscation","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What the XOR encoding actually protects against, and what it doesn’t."}]},"doc://TightlipCore/documentation/TightlipCore/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/TightlipCore\/documentation\/TightlipCore\/GettingStarted","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/tightlipcore\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started with Tightlip","abstract":[{"text":"Add the plugin to a target, drop in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Secrets.yml","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and start reading secrets at compile time.","type":"text"}]}}}